  "question": {
    "text": "An infinitely long positively charged straight thread has a linear charge density $\\lambda \\mathrm{Cm}^{-1}$. An electron revolves along a circular path having axis along the length of the wire. The graph that correctly represents the variation of the kinetic energy of electron as a function of radius of circular path from the wire is :",
